; a long, thin, rigid structural element — vertical or horizontal.
; vertical pole: flagpole, lamppost, column, pillar.
; horizontal pole: beam, rod, axle, rail.
; a pole is a one-dimensional structural object in 3d space:
; it has length but its cross-section is negligible at everyday scale.
; 
; in physics: the pole is the simplest rigid body.
; a pendulum is a mass on a pole (or string).
; a lever is a horizontal pole with a fulcrum.
; torque: force applied perpendicular to a pole at a distance r → τ = r × F.
; 
; in 3d/pratibimba: a cylinder mesh with high length/width ratio.

(kosha pole
  (vishesa structures-varga common-sense-varga)
  (swarupa rigid elongated)
  (yukta torque lever domain-3d)
  (sthita solid))
